    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I found on [this stack overflow answer](https://stackoverflow.com/a/426910/4476484) that <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>-<kbd>q</kbd> from normal mode enters visual block mode. It works from `nvim -u NONE`.\n\nThere is no neovim help entry for `:help ctrl-q`.\n\nThere are a few mentions of <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>-<kbd>q</kbd> that I found throughout the neovim help files, but none of them mention that it puts you in visual block mode. `:help visual-block` doesn't mention <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>-<kbd>q</kbd> anywhere in the file.\n\nIs this intentional?\n\n### System\nNeovim v0.12.4\nUbuntu 24.04 on WSL2 on Windows 11",
